hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1543","I am Bundar, Na Yahya, and Muhammad bin Jaafar, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, and Al-Sana’ani narrated to us, Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, narrated to us, on the authority of Division. H. Salam bin Junada, narrated to us by Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, said: I heard Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and said: “Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of the completion of the prayer.” This is the hadith of Bundar. Salam bin Junada said: On the authority of Qatada, who said: “Part of the good prayer is to establish the row.”"
